# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Jinzhe Zeng et al. (2023). DeePMD-kit v2: A software package for deep potential models.
#   The Journal of Chemical Physics. doi:10.1063/5.0155600  arXiv:2304.09409v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2304.09409v1 (sha256 cafd51bff7d1be6b...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 177 (Software/implementation). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
#
# Encoding scope: the DeePMD-kit v2 package as an implementation of the
# Deep Potential method, and the benchmark of Table I: 40 models (five
# descriptor types, double and single precision) trained on six published
# data sets, with validation MAE and RMSE for energies and forces. The
# descriptor type and precision are run settings. Training and MD
# timings (Tables II and III) are not encoded. Read from the arXiv
# preprint (v1).

