###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# The paper reports no training-cost or inference-cost figures.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - All five descriptor types (local frame, DeepPot-SE two-body, the two hybrids, and the attention-based se_atten, known elsewhere as DPA-1) are encoded under the one registry method DeePMD with the descriptor as a setting, since they are options of one package; if the attention-based descriptor should be a method of its own, that is one registry row and a re-pointing of ten runs.
# - cutoffRadius is 6 A (9 A for OC2M) as stated; in the two hybrid descriptors the se_e2_a part uses 4 A, which is not encoded separately. The se_atten settings M = 16 and two attention layers and the three-body embedding net (2,4,8) are not encoded.
# - The data sets are published ones; sizes and reference levels are not restated in the paper, so the data-set nodes carry no reference calculation. Table I values are validation errors (5% split). The text quotes the best water result as 0.689 meV/atom and 39.2 meV/A, consistent with the loc_frame FP32 column.
# - Training speeds (Table II, ms/step on five hardware platforms) and MD speeds (Table III, microseconds per step per atom, including compressed models and the FPGA NVNMD) are not encoded; they would fit mlips:inferenceTimePerAtom for the water, Cu and HEA models once a hardware choice is made. Read from the arXiv v1 preprint.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).

